# ESP32-S3 gun detection firmware

First functional version: all sensing circuits, the ESP32-S3, GPS and Wi-Fi remain active.
No light/deep-sleep logic is enabled yet.

## Pin assignment

| Function | GPIO |
|---|---:|
| Microphone ADC | 8 |
| MMA7361 X/Y/Z | 4 / 5 / 6 |
| MMA7361 SLEEP | 7 (HIGH = active) |
| GPS EN / PPS | 9 / 10 |
| ESP32 UART TX / RX | 17 / 18 |

## Modules

- `voice_detection`: continuous 1 kHz sampling, 10 ms frame P2P/RMS/energy-rise detection.
- `vibrate_detection`: 1 kHz three-axis sampling, baseline, magnitude and jerk detection.
- `shot_detector`: time-window fusion and duplicate-shot suppression.
- `gps_manager`: continuous NMEA parsing through UART1.
- `wifi_transport`: non-blocking connection management and UDP/JSON event queue.

## Configuration

Edit `include/system_config.h` before hardware/network testing:

- Calibrate the voice and vibration thresholds from serial output.
- Set `WIFI_SSID`, `WIFI_PASSWORD`, `UPPER_COMPUTER_HOST` and port.
- Verify the GPS baud rate and that its EN pin is active HIGH.

With Wi-Fi settings left empty, upload is disabled but detection, GPS and serial diagnostics continue.

The firmware synchronizes the ESP32 system RTC from valid GPS UTC date/time. UDP status and
shot packets include `timestamp` in `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS` format and `timestampValid`.
The RTC continues running while Wi-Fi is disconnected. After a full power loss, a valid GPS
time is required to initialize the calendar clock again; this board configuration has no
separate battery-backed RTC module. When no valid RTC time is available, the timestamp is empty
and `timestampValid` is false. The monitor uses the device timestamp for its display and CSV
when available, and falls back to the computer receive time otherwise.

Each voice or vibration trigger is also queued and uploaded as its own `detection` UDP event
(`detectionType` is `voice` or `vibration`). Status packets include cumulative
`voiceDetectionCount` and `vibrationDetectionCount` values since boot; the monitor displays both
counts and the latest event details separately. Fused detections continue to upload as `shot`
events.

Static roll/pitch estimates use the MMA7361 axes after a separate 2-second startup calibration.
Keep the sensor level and motionless during this calibration. The original 300-sample vibration
calibration and vibration detection continue independently. The status packet reports
`tilt.rollDeg` and `tilt.pitchDeg`; these accelerometer-only angles are intended for static or
slow tilt and are affected by firing and other linear acceleration.

## Build

```sh
pio run
```

Serial monitor baud rate: 115200.
